# Check the x402 seller before the agent pays

When code pays an x402 endpoint, put a seller check in front of the signer.

- New buyer code: use `createBuyerFetch` from `twzrd-x402-gate` (npm). It requires a per-call price cap
  (`maxPricePerCall`) and a payTo allowlist (`allowedRecipients`), and it runs a free preflight before signing.
  It fails closed: a check that cannot answer refuses, and so does a network the scorer marks unscored.
- An existing `@x402/core` client: `installTwzrdAutoGate(client, { refuseWashFlagged: true })`.
- On `block`, do not pay. On `warn`, stay under the cap. A seller with `wash_flagged: true` is refused.
  `wash_flagged: null` means the seller was never evaluated, not that it is clean.

To check one seller by hand, use this plugin's `twzrd-intel` MCP tools, or run `/check-seller`:
`evaluate_x402_resource` takes the resource URL and `get_merchant_card` takes the payTo address. Neither tool
pays or needs a key. An `unknown` decision from `evaluate_x402_resource` means the URL issued no 402, so nothing
was evaluated; it is not a green light.
